# TCR07 : OCTO1182 : Test a CancelRequest that arrives while the cross reference metadata of a plan is set cancels the query
# When the plan of a query uses a cross reference, emit_physical_plan() runs M code (the _ydboctoxrefMetadata call-in)
# that sets the name of the cross reference global in ^%ydbAIMOctoCache(table,column,"location"). A CancelRequest that
# arrived while that M code ran unwound it before the node was set, and the rocto server then terminated abnormally
# (an assert failure in tmpl_key_source_aim in a Debug build) when the rest of the plan was generated. The rocto server
# below sends itself the CancelRequest signal right before that M code runs.
# Run 2 queries through psql (simple query protocol) on the same connection.
# Query 1 needs a cross reference on names.firstname. Expect it to be canceled.
ERROR:  canceling statement due to user request
# Query 2 needs no cross reference. Expect 1 row, which shows the rocto server is still running
# and that the cancel of query 1 does not affect the next query.
 id | firstname | lastname 
----+-----------+----------
  3 | Lord      | Nikon
(1 row)

# Run a SELECT that needs a cross reference on names.lastname through JDBC (extended query protocol).
# Expect the query to be canceled.
SQL State: 57014
ERROR: canceling statement due to user request
# Run the 2 canceled queries through octo, which has no test hook. Expect 2 rows from each query.
id|firstname|lastname
0|Zero|Cool
5|Zero|Cool
(2 rows)
id|firstname|lastname
0|Zero|Cool
5|Zero|Cool
(2 rows)
